---
import RelatedLinks from '../../RelatedLinks.astro';
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--peach" id="overview">
    <div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
      <div class="page-hero__copy reveal">
        <span class="ey">PunchOut solutions</span>
        <h1>Start with the buyer problem your Shopify business needs to solve.</h1>
        <p class="lead">An enterprise customer may require PunchOut, one store may need to serve several buyers, or several stores may need one operating view. Find the model that fits your supplier program.</p>
        <div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="#models">Find your use case &darr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/book-demo/">Discuss a buyer requirement</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual reveal" aria-label="Supplier and buyer connection models">
        <div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Supplier models</span><b>One platform</b></div>
        <div class="visual-flow">
          <div class="visual-step is-accent"><i>01</i><span><strong>One supplier store</strong><small>Several enterprise buyers</small></span></div>
          <div class="visual-step is-lavender"><i>02</i><span><strong>Several stores</strong><small>Buyer-specific catalog access</small></span></div>
          <div class="visual-step is-peach"><i>03</i><span><strong>One transaction view</strong><small>PunchOut through invoice</small></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="models"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Choose a use case</span><h2>Different starting points. A connected buyer workflow.</h2><p class="lead">Each solution addresses a distinct operating question and links to the product capability behind it.</p></div>
    <div class="related-grid">
      <a class="related-card reveal" href="/solutions/b2b-suppliers/"><span>Supplier opportunity</span><h3>For Shopify B2B suppliers</h3><p>Support a procurement-led customer using the Shopify store you already operate.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="related-card reveal" href="/solutions/enterprise-customer-onboarding/"><span>New buyer</span><h3>Enterprise buyer onboarding</h3><p>Collect buyer requirements, assign catalog access, test the flow and launch.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="related-card reveal" href="/solutions/one-store-multiple-buyers/"><span>Shared storefront</span><h3>One store, multiple buyers</h3><p>Serve several enterprise connections from a single Shopify catalog.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="related-card reveal" href="/solutions/multi-store-commerce/"><span>Several storefronts</span><h3>Multi-store commerce</h3><p>Map different buyers and catalogs while viewing activity centrally.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="related-card reveal" href="/solutions/ecommerce-agencies/"><span>Client project</span><h3>For Shopify agencies</h3><p>Scope procurement connectivity alongside a client’s existing commerce build.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="related-card reveal" href="/enterprise/"><span>Larger program</span><h3>Enterprise supplier programs</h3><p>Plan several buyers, stores and procurement requirements together.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="sec soft" id="path"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Implementation path</span><h2>Connect the store. Add the buyer. Test the transaction.</h2><p class="lead">PunchOut Central uses Shopify or Shopify Plus for the supplier catalog and supports cXML and OCI procurement workflows.</p></div>
    <div class="simple-steps">
      <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">01</span><h3>Keep your store</h3><p>Use the existing supplier storefront instead of building a separate PunchOut catalog.</p></article>
      <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">02</span><h3>Set buyer access</h3><p>Choose the store and relevant collections or catalog access for each buyer.</p></article>
      <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">03</span><h3>Validate the flow</h3><p>Test session launch, cart return and the approved purchase order path.</p></article>
      <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">04</span><h3>Follow the journey</h3><p>Track the transaction through Shopify order creation and invoice generation.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <RelatedLinks source="/solutions/" heading="Explore the capabilities behind each solution" />
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Next step</span><h2>Show us the buyer and store relationship.</h2><p class="lead">We can discuss procurement requirements, catalog access and connection pricing.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Request a demo &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/pricing/">Compare plans</a></div></div></section>
</main>
